============================================================
1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
============================================================

This project implements a C-based simulation of the memory subsystem
specified in Question #1 of DSTN Assignment #2.

A memory reference follows:

    CPU Virtual Address
            |
            v
           TLB
            |
      TLB Hit / Miss
            |
            v
        Page Table
            |
      Present / Page Fault
            |
            v
      Physical Frame
            |
            v
     Physical Address
            |
            v
           L1
            |
        Hit / Miss
            |
            v
           L2
            |
        Hit / Miss
            |
            v
       Main Memory

The implementation uses separate ADTs for each major subsystem.
Address decomposition uses bitwise masking and shifting rather than
division/modulo based field extraction.


============================================================
2. QUESTION #1 CONFIGURATION IMPLEMENTED
============================================================

Paging:
- Pure paging
- Page size = 1 KB
- Frame size = 1 KB
- First two pages of every process are pre-paged into main memory
- Remaining pages are demand-loaded
- Global replacement
- Main-memory replacement policy: LRU
- Page tables reside in main memory and are not cached

TLB:
- 32 entries
- PID/identifier stored in each entry
- Lookup using PID + VPN
- PID-specific invalidation on process termination
- Individual PID/VPN invalidation when a page is evicted

L1 Cache:
- 4 KB
- 16 B block
- 4-way set associative
- 64 sets
- Way prediction
- Virtually tagged
- Physically indexed
- Write-through
- Look-through
- LRU square-matrix replacement

L2 Cache:
- 32 KB
- 32 B block
- 8-way set associative
- 128 sets
- Write-back
- Look-aside
- LRU-counter replacement
- Dirty-bit handling and writeback on dirty eviction

Main Memory:
- 32 MB
- 32768 physical frames
- Global LRU frame replacement
- Per-process resident-page lower and upper limits are tracked


============================================================
3. ADDRESS BIT MAPPING
============================================================

Page size = 1 KB = 2^10 bytes

Virtual address:

    +---------------------------+------------------+
    |            VPN            |   Page Offset    |
    +---------------------------+------------------+
                                   10 bits

Implemented as:

    VPN         = VA >> 10
    Page Offset = VA & 0x3FF

Physical address:

    PA = (PFN << 10) | PageOffset

L1:
- 16 B block -> 4 block-offset bits
- 64 sets -> 6 set bits

    L1 offset      = PA[3:0]
    L1 set         = PA[9:4]
    L1 virtual tag = VA[31:10]

L2:
- 32 B block -> 5 block-offset bits
- 128 sets -> 7 set bits

    L2 offset = PA[4:0]
    L2 set    = PA[11:5]

The current implementation uses the remaining upper physical-address
bits as the L2 tag.


