============================================================
7. PROGRAM STRUCTURE
============================================================

A normal access executes the following sequence:

1. CPU supplies PID, virtual address and READ/WRITE operation.
2. VA is split into VPN and page offset using masks/shifts.
3. TLB is searched using PID + VPN.
4. On TLB miss, the process page table is consulted.
5. If the PTE is absent, a page fault is generated.
6. Physical memory allocates a free frame where possible; otherwise
   global LRU replacement is used while respecting page limits.
7. PTE/TLB mappings are updated.
8. PA is constructed as PFN | page offset.
9. L1 is accessed with a physical set index and virtual tag.
10. Way prediction is attempted before the remaining ways are searched.
11. On L1 miss, L2 is accessed.
12. On L2 miss, the block is obtained from main memory.
13. L1 writes use write-through behaviour.
14. L2 writes use write-back behaviour and dirty bits.
15. Dirty L2 victims are written back on replacement.


